1:# notify-digest
2:
3:A small cron job that pulls a handful of feeds, filters the items per channel,
4:and sends each channel a digest.
5:
6:## Running
7:
8:```sh
9:cp config.example.toml config.toml
10:python3 digest.py --config config.toml --db digest.sqlite3
11:```
12:
13:`--dry-run` prints what would be sent instead of sending it. It does not
14:consult the delivery ledger, so it always shows the full current feed.
15:
16:Requires Python 3.11+ (uses `tomllib`). No third-party dependencies.
17:
18:## Choosing what goes in a digest
19:
20:The feeds mostly repeat their current contents on every poll, so without
21:memory every 15-minute tick would re-send the same stories. A channel only
22:gets items it has **never been sent before**. Two occurrences count as the
23:same item when they have the same source *and* the same link with its query
24:string and fragment stripped — never by provider id: the wire provider
25:regenerates its `guid` whenever an item is edited, and newsroom appends a
26:rotating `utm_campaign=` to its urls, so ids and raw urls change for stories
27:people have already seen (that is exactly the spam this rule removes).
28:Matching is per channel: an item matching two channels is sent once to each,
29:and a brand-new channel is backfilled with everything currently in the
30:feeds.
31:
32:History lives in the SQLite file (`--db`): `items` archives every fetch,
33:`delivered` is the ledger of what each channel has received. Items are added
34:to the ledger *after* a successful send, so if a send fails the run aborts
35:and the next tick retries the items that never got through. Deleting the db
36:file (or its `delivered` table) resets everyone's memory.
37:
38:## Layout
39:
40:| File | Purpose |
41:| --- | --- |
42:| `digest.py` | CLI entry point, the per-run loop |
43:| `feeds.py` | Fetching and normalising the three feed formats |
44:| `store.py` | SQLite archive of everything seen + per-channel delivery ledger |
45:| `render.py` | Digest text |
46:| `channels.py` | Delivery (stdout, webhook) |
47:
48:The `fixtures/` directory holds two snapshots of the feeds taken at different
49:times, so you can work on this without network access. Point the config at
50:`snapshot-a` or `snapshot-b`.
51:
52:## Deployment
53:
54:Runs from cron on the utility box:
55:
56:```
57:*/15 * * * * cd /srv/notify-digest && python3 digest.py >> /var/log/digest.log 2>&1
58:```
